#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434793} :activity/id #uuid "f7bf5624-eb3d-524c-adc4-5621731bf40f" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049462 :topic/id #uuid "f7488799-2322-5ff9-8065-6852954f5eb5" :topic/math-academy-id 3819} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434791 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17453e7d-2501-500c-988d-632cc6dfbc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368922} {:answer/id #uuid "3e7fa423-ce11-5e4b-941d-b20daa102519" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368923} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf839ad-4dca-5536-a5e6-2102abbf3175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$8$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368924} {:answer/id #uuid "d0871187-035d-52b5-b781-f70eaa3bf24c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368925} {:answer/id #uuid "0183a8ef-a247-5fec-a72f-23430bb57861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368926}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368925} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbd50738-594a-50f0-9455-2e79aec8430d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368921}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "80bd1a5b-eef3-57d3-b7a8-ea1d67708737" :question/math-academy-id "q-95364" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -6 \\\\ -6 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}10-\\lambda  & -6 \\\\ -6 & 10-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (10-\\lambda )(10-\\lambda )-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda +100-36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda +64 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -16) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =16,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{16}=4 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0b89f8b4-c620-53dc-98a8-673f79519cb0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434794}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434792 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5aacda77-04a2-5890-a544-02a590c4abbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368908} {:answer/id #uuid "d7d351a9-304d-59f9-bb2a-64ac42ed426b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$5$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368909} {:answer/id #uuid "37198688-7720-5bf5-9d97-18a4fc4f1eae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$25$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368910} {:answer/id #uuid "11993b50-f9b2-5859-af25-cf8175b4ff5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368911} {:answer/id #uuid "4633659c-497d-54ae-9280-c13bf99f6b0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$25$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368912}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186368909} :answer-field/id #uuid "08930f82-1a1a-57e2-874c-8663b93ed935" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186368907}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "bc0c7469-fdf7-5096-ab3b-9c5617b672e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-95316" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}9-\\lambda  & 12 \\\\ 12 & 16-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (9-\\lambda )(16-\\lambda )-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda -16\\lambda +144-144 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-25\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -25) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =25,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{25}=5 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "579fd70b-a4f5-506a-a516-6e2012961957" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434791}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434793 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184878 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ea50afa6-cf48-5a28-88f9-d3e965d42d17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$9$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404740} {:answer/id #uuid "58501d70-837f-5aaa-b030-23424dea0d8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{10}$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404741} {:answer/id #uuid "5b30f13e-19e7-5a1b-8f5a-9d9ae0821275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$3$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404742} {:answer/id #uuid "09c94f4b-6a80-5db2-b8a4-38435a2f0752" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$3$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404743} {:answer/id #uuid "185ef847-122c-55fe-afa8-642c48c26e9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$10$ and $0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404744}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404743} :answer-field/id #uuid "d1608723-f0ef-5251-b5a7-f10ee403c96e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404739}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1a7c1d3e-ea07-5462-b92b-00ccbee66e53" :question/math-academy-id "q-94982" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +25-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +9 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "7fbe2269-e57f-5576-bab4-acdbbf9470a5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434792}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434794 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57ba2282-d4ab-5fbf-9130-d06a2eed65a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385854} {:answer/id #uuid "b45ecc1a-07a7-50a1-a446-cf4a96064ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2,\\,2,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385855} {:answer/id #uuid "f1a83de7-3a30-52e2-a29e-09bdd3418bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5,\\,2,\\,1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385856} {:answer/id #uuid "01e6f9da-3643-528a-9879-9df01fb0203d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9,\\,4,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385857} {:answer/id #uuid "d58280f6-ca95-52bf-80d9-6a8986b3c8bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4,\\,1,\\,0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385858}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186385854} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a01643e-564d-5068-bf87-5773a11495bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385853}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "63c30a7c-7d2d-5a6c-adcf-5b929543dd1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-95369" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 8-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )((5-\\lambda )(8-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{0}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a3a70805-ef62-5a01-8da2-b71b9b73402a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434795}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434795 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383410 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81eab9b6-2c22-56c2-8b09-bb7ba88bb023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4,$ $2,$ $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383412} {:answer/id #uuid "45fdf803-5c63-5fd1-98ac-6d33e693cf05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4,$ $3,$ $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383413} {:answer/id #uuid "8b43b2a5-0f26-58bc-89b2-44f5ea0b5aee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$4,$ $4,$ $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383414} {:answer/id #uuid "e057365e-ebcb-5deb-8291-d5e0f828271e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$3,$ $2,$ $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383415} {:answer/id #uuid "8afd4451-cbc1-5888-a4c6-5aa0879d00a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$2,$ $2,$ $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383416}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383415} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d2e9298-f7ae-583b-b56c-2427f10af7e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383411}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5a2eadfc-214c-5e6d-a649-83f2e39bac57" :question/math-academy-id "q-139505" :question/problem "What are the singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nFirst, we calculate ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the characteristic equation of ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|{A}^{T}\\,A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )((5-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-16) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +9) & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,4,\\,1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the singular values of $A$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sigma }_{1} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{1}}=\\sqrt{9}=3 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{2} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{2}}=\\sqrt{4}=2 \\\\ {\\sigma }_{3} & =\\sqrt{{\\lambda }_{3}}=\\sqrt{1}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b00be353-af3c-5697-8948-437078c60988"}] :activity/title "Computing the Singular Values of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434790}]}
